SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only

Added to the Store package's manifest (appx.customExtensionsPath in src/artise/build/builderConfig.ts). The
Microsoft Store build starts at login through this, on by default: a packaged app can't use the registry Run key
Element's auto-launch writes. People turn it off in Windows' Settings → Apps → Startup.
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/schemas/appxpackage/uapmanifestschema/element-uap5-startuptask
-->
        <desktop:Extension Category="windows.startupTask" Executable="app\Artise.exe" EntryPoint="Windows.FullTrustApplication">
          <desktop:StartupTask TaskId="ArtiseStartup" Enabled="true" DisplayName="Artise" />
        </desktop:Extension>
